@ChineseBurrito93 Nah, mate. This kind of argument is not going to get you anywhere. You cannot provide any tangible evidence for any specific civilian deaths that Putin has specifically caused.

Then your argument rests on "well, he started a war in which thousands of civilians died". That is true, but that is the reality of war. The war in Ukraine is by far the most "civilian-friendly" of all the wars, possibly ever, at least on the Russian side. You cannot argue that - the civilian-to-military death ratio in Ukraine is ludicrously low.

Then your only argument is "Yeah, but he still started a war, and thousands of civilians still died", to which the response is simple: when one is put into a situation with no good options, they will take the one that is best for their chances of survival. I can point to Trump, Ursula, Netanyahu and the clown in Kiev himself as people who also have caused thousands of civilian deaths. The main difference with Putin - they did not need to, and they do not care. This last argument I am making is a complex one, happy to argue it, but I doubt you will want to go there.

