snippet.textDisplay:
@dllemm "Unitree and others will be producing over 1 million humanoids per year"
Order of magnitude off. Unitree itself is aiming for 20,000 humanoids, and they are the biggest player. All the others in China may or may not add up to 100k this year, and much fewer in the US despite competitive technology. It's basically just China and the US globally for this. Most of the volume has been industry; for the market to take off they'd need home adoption, and that's currently a big if.

The US does make and use a lot of industrial robots (around a million installed), just like China and its 2 million - but the vast majority aren't humanoid.

